This section will cover the scenario related questions that are asked in the DevOps interview.

Scenario :-

You are a DevOps engineer configuring a Kubernetes Deployment for a web application. The deployment must support graceful shutdown so that in-flight requests can complete before pods are 
terminated during rolling updates or scaling events.

Current State
You have a single Kubernetes manifest file:

deployment.yaml — A basic Deployment for the web application that currently lacks graceful shutdown configuration.
Requirements
Graceful Shutdown

Configure the Deployment's pod spec to allow sufficient time for in-flight requests to complete before the pod is forcefully terminated:
Set terminationGracePeriodSeconds to at least 30 seconds at the pod spec level (i.e., under spec.template.spec).

This ensures that when Kubernetes sends a SIGTERM to the container, the pod is given enough time to drain connections and shut down cleanly.

Constraints
The Deployment name must remain web-app
The application listens on port 8080.
Use the image codility/web-app:1.0 (or any qualified image with a specific version tag).

Answer :-

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: web-app
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: web-app
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: web-app
    spec:
      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30  ==> Added the " terminationGracePeriodSeconds" to set the graceful termination.
      containers:
        - name: web-app
          image: codility/web-app:1.0    ==> Image added for the container
          ports:
            - containerPort: 8080
